{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"060ecd6f14eb4c350f90ce78c69b7656","RawContent":"Okay Perfect!!!  Thanks Sandy!  I was thinking the same outline.  I appreciate your help!! \n \n   \n -Amy \n [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]Sandy Planner[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Dear AmyG: Sorry for not getting back to you earlier!! \n \n The ceremony  at 5:00 pm , I really suggest to you  give at least 30 minutes for pictures ....and then have the cocktail hour ... you may request Anel or Ramon s[b]erve at the end of ceremony ,[\/b] either sparkling wine or  your signature drink...it is always refreshing after ceremony have something to drink...and then  30 minutes after  start the cocktail hour... \n \n I would said  6:00 pm for cocktail hour  and 7:00 Reception starts...please note that most of the time the wedding couple miss half of the cocktail hour because the  photographer make photosession only with the couple. \n \n You can request during your first meeting a taste for signature drink ...if you can include a picture in the planning form it is VERY appreciated jeje :) \n \n Sandy  \n \n \n   \n \n \n[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1584664,"PostDate":1329796880,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Okay Perfect!!!\u00a0 Thanks Sandy!\u00a0 I was thinking the same outline.\u00a0 I appreciate your help!!<\/p> <p> <br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <p> -Amy<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>Sandy Planner<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Dear AmyG: Sorry for not getting back to you earlier!!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The ceremony \u00a0at 5:00 pm , I really suggest to you \u00a0give at least 30 minutes for pictures ....and then have the cocktail hour ... you may request Anel or Ramon s<strong>erve at the end of ceremony ,<\/strong> either sparkling wine or \u00a0your signature drink...it is always refreshing after ceremony have something to drink...and then \u00a030 minutes after \u00a0start the cocktail hour...<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I would said \u00a06:00 pm for cocktail hour \u00a0and 7:00 Reception starts...please note that most of the time the wedding couple miss half of the cocktail hour because the \u00a0photographer make photosession only with the couple.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> You can request during your first meeting a taste for signature drink ...if you can include a picture in the planning form it is VERY appreciated jeje <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Sandy\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ladybug1280@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1284746058,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232417.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AmyG","Id":232417,"Name":"AmyG","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"cc26ad5ccf6eacaffeb7572b58d6d743","RawContent":"ps31, \n \n CONGRATS!!  I am so happy for you!  It&#039;s great to hear that you had a great time and it all went well.  I am sure I will have a question, or two...or three for you but I think I&#039;m set for now.  \n Enjoy being married!!!  :-) \n \n -Amy \n [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]ps31[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Well I just got back from our wedding at Now last weekend.  It was WONDERFUL!!  The staff there was amazing and I didn&#039;t have to worry about anything the day of the wedding.  I had been communicating with Anel the entire time, but Ramon took care over our wedding once we got there.  I was really impressed with the service he provided and all the information he was able to remember;)  I absolutely[b] loved [\/b]the flowers we got and we used their florists. \n \n As far as your last discussion about when do to cocktail hour\/reception\/etc, I didn&#039;t have any idea when to schedule that stuff either.  Once we had our meeting with Ramon he lead us in the right directions for a time line.  I wouldn&#039;t worry too much about the planning forum, it doesn&#039;t seem like they look at it until shortly before you arrive and you can change a lot of things once you get there.  We had our ceremony at 4:30 and didn&#039;t start the cocktail hour until 5:30.  We did some pictures after the ceremony so from 5-5:45.  So the guests had plenty of down time to enjoy cocktail hour before dinner was served.  I think any more time would have been too much standing around time.  Like Sandy said my groom and I missed half of the cocktail hour doing other things, I didn&#039;t even get to try all the tasty cocktail treats!:) \n \n I&#039;ll post a link to some of the pictures.  The resort was beautiful!  If anyone has any questions feel free to ask, this forum was super helpful for me so I would love to help out anyone else needing reassurance;)  If you picked Now Sapphire, I don&#039;t think you&#039;ll be disappointed with your wedding day! \n \n [url=\"http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148\"]http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148[\/url][\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1584666,"PostDate":1329797040,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <br \/> ps31,<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> CONGRATS!!\u00a0 I am so happy for you!\u00a0 It's great to hear that you had a great time and it all went well.\u00a0 I am sure I will have a question, or two...or three for you but I think I'm set for now.\u00a0<\/p> <p> Enjoy being married!!!\u00a0 :-)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> -Amy<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>ps31<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Well I just got back from our wedding at Now last weekend.\u00a0 It was WONDERFUL!!\u00a0 The staff there was amazing and I didn't have to worry about anything the day of the wedding.\u00a0 I had been communicating with Anel the entire time, but Ramon took care over our wedding once we got there.\u00a0 I was really impressed with the service he provided and all the information he was able to remember;)\u00a0 I absolutely<strong> loved <\/strong>the flowers we got and we used their florists.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> As far as your last discussion about when do to cocktail hour\/reception\/etc, I didn't have any idea when to schedule that stuff either.\u00a0 Once we had our meeting with Ramon he lead us in the right directions for a time line.\u00a0 I wouldn't worry too much about the planning forum, it doesn't seem like they look at it until shortly before you arrive and you can change a lot of things once you get there.\u00a0 We had our ceremony at 4:30 and didn't start the cocktail hour until 5:30.\u00a0 We did some pictures after the ceremony so from 5-5:45.\u00a0 So the guests had plenty of down time to enjoy cocktail hour before dinner was served.\u00a0 I think any more time would have been too much standing around time.\u00a0 Like Sandy said my groom and I missed half of the cocktail hour doing other things, I didn't even get to try all the tasty cocktail treats!<img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I'll post a link to some of the pictures.\u00a0 The resort was beautiful!\u00a0 If anyone has any questions feel free to ask, this forum was super helpful for me so I would love to help out anyone else needing reassurance;)\u00a0 If you picked Now Sapphire, I don't think you'll be disappointed with your wedding day!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148<\/a><\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ladybug1280@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1284746058,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232417.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AmyG","Id":232417,"Name":"AmyG","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"22807e94162272fa2499e36eba188721","RawContent":"Dear PS31 , Congratulations for your wedding  YES Ramon is a great coordinator....as you said many of the little thing will be discussed upon arrival  ...I really love Now Sapphire as wedding location....something I really would like to share with everyone is that the planning form is SUPER important for  Ramon and Anel  they have to send monthly reports  for everyone to plan  all the food orders , the staff to work in your receptions , for the musicians , for the DJ etc.... it is really important they have on time the planning , as you well said  little details will be discussed upon  arrival but they need some important information from the planning before....they have to put together 16 different areas oin the resort ;)   \n \n Congratulations again. \n \n Sandy \n \n \n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]ps31[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Well I just got back from our wedding at Now last weekend.  It was WONDERFUL!!  The staff there was amazing and I didn&#039;t have to worry about anything the day of the wedding.  I had been communicating with Anel the entire time, but Ramon took care over our wedding once we got there.  I was really impressed with the service he provided and all the information he was able to remember;)  I absolutely[b] loved [\/b]the flowers we got and we used their florists. \n \n As far as your last discussion about when do to cocktail hour\/reception\/etc, I didn&#039;t have any idea when to schedule that stuff either.  Once we had our meeting with Ramon he lead us in the right directions for a time line.  I wouldn&#039;t worry too much about the planning forum, it doesn&#039;t seem like they look at it until shortly before you arrive and you can change a lot of things once you get there.  We had our ceremony at 4:30 and didn&#039;t start the cocktail hour until 5:30.  We did some pictures after the ceremony so from 5-5:45.  So the guests had plenty of down time to enjoy cocktail hour before dinner was served.  I think any more time would have been too much standing around time.  Like Sandy said my groom and I missed half of the cocktail hour doing other things, I didn&#039;t even get to try all the tasty cocktail treats!:) \n \n I&#039;ll post a link to some of the pictures.  The resort was beautiful!  If anyone has any questions feel free to ask, this forum was super helpful for me so I would love to help out anyone else needing reassurance;)  If you picked Now Sapphire, I don&#039;t think you&#039;ll be disappointed with your wedding day! \n \n [url=\"http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148\"]http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148[\/url][\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1584811,"PostDate":1329844497,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Dear PS31 , Congratulations for your wedding \u00a0YES Ramon is a great coordinator....as you said many of the little thing will be discussed upon arrival \u00a0...I really love Now Sapphire as wedding location....something I really would like to share with everyone is that the planning form is SUPER important for \u00a0Ramon and Anel \u00a0they have to send monthly reports \u00a0for everyone to plan \u00a0all the food orders , the staff to work in your receptions , for the musicians , for the DJ etc.... it is really important they have on time the planning , as you well said \u00a0little details will be discussed upon \u00a0arrival but they need some important information from the planning before....they have to put together 16 different areas oin the resort <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Congratulations again.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Sandy<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>ps31<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Well I just got back from our wedding at Now last weekend.\u00a0 It was WONDERFUL!!\u00a0 The staff there was amazing and I didn't have to worry about anything the day of the wedding.\u00a0 I had been communicating with Anel the entire time, but Ramon took care over our wedding once we got there.\u00a0 I was really impressed with the service he provided and all the information he was able to remember;)\u00a0 I absolutely<strong> loved <\/strong>the flowers we got and we used their florists.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> As far as your last discussion about when do to cocktail hour\/reception\/etc, I didn't have any idea when to schedule that stuff either.\u00a0 Once we had our meeting with Ramon he lead us in the right directions for a time line.\u00a0 I wouldn't worry too much about the planning forum, it doesn't seem like they look at it until shortly before you arrive and you can change a lot of things once you get there.\u00a0 We had our ceremony at 4:30 and didn't start the cocktail hour until 5:30.\u00a0 We did some pictures after the ceremony so from 5-5:45.\u00a0 So the guests had plenty of down time to enjoy cocktail hour before dinner was served.\u00a0 I think any more time would have been too much standing around time.\u00a0 Like Sandy said my groom and I missed half of the cocktail hour doing other things, I didn't even get to try all the tasty cocktail treats!<img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I'll post a link to some of the pictures.\u00a0 The resort was beautiful!\u00a0 If anyone has any questions feel free to ask, this forum was super helpful for me so I would love to help out anyone else needing reassurance;)\u00a0 If you picked Now Sapphire, I don't think you'll be disappointed with your wedding day!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/sbphotoblog.com\/?p=2148<\/a><\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"info@ultimatemexicoweddings.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1321993668,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-247948.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":86,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Sandy Planner","Id":247948,"Name":"Sandy Planner","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5a02309575cda0677d8e1a6788ae111a","RawContent":"[quote name=\"HeatherViolet\"]\n&lt;p&gt; Ryan- Where did you end up finding sashes so cheap?&amp;nbsp; I looked at Hobby Lobby and the tule stuff just comes in a roll, so I don&#039;t know how much I would need.&amp;nbsp; We too are looking for aqua.... but I am also looking for orange.&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; What are you guys doing for decos during the ceremony?&amp;nbsp; Getting flowers from the resort, or making something for the \"pew bows\"?&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; How about the reception?&amp;nbsp; Any decorations there?&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Heather&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;[\/quote] Hi Heather, Just to let you know we received our sashes the other day and they are really nice. I don&#039;t know why the eBay link says they are in Hong Kong as they were shipped from Kentucky. We bought 27 aqua and 27 purple.","Attachments":[],"Id":1587227,"PostDate":1330290961,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class='ipsBlockquote' data-author=\"HeatherViolet\" url=\"\/t\/74418\/now&#045;sapphire&#045;weddings&#045;formerly&#045;paradisus&#045;riviera\/250#post_1732615\"><p><p> Ryan- Where did you end up finding sashes so cheap?\u00a0 I looked at Hobby Lobby and the tule stuff just comes in a roll, so I don't know how much I would need.\u00a0 We too are looking for aqua.... but I am also looking for orange.<\/p><p> \u00a0<\/p><p> What are you guys doing for decos during the ceremony?\u00a0 Getting flowers from the resort, or making something for the \"pew bows\"?<\/p><p> How about the reception?\u00a0 Any decorations there?<\/p><p> \u00a0<\/p><p> Heather<\/p><p> \u00a0<\/p><\/p><\/blockquote> Hi Heather, Just to let you know we received our sashes the other day and they are really nice. I don't know why the eBay link says they are in Hong Kong as they were shipped from Kentucky. We bought 27 aqua and 27 purple.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ryan@panthersgrad.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1307990680,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-241083.jpg?_r=1388290366","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":255,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"RFinger","Id":241083,"Name":"RFinger","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f6d008f4e71fcfd4a79465cb9cd760d9","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Hello All&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It&#039;s looks &lt;strong&gt;amazing&lt;\/strong&gt;!)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we&#039;re shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; One thing we&#039;re already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons?&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; We&#039;ve been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I&#039;ve just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Thanks and best regards&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; - TK&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1588450,"PostDate":1330539623,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Hello All<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It's looks <strong>amazing<\/strong>!)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we're shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> One thing we're already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons?<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We've been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I've just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thanks and best regards<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> - TK<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"thomask122184@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1325865744,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-249443.png?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":118,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ThomasK","Id":249443,"Name":"ThomasK","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"996de60bd27bc409d24a2fd55ffa015f","RawContent":"Hi TK! \n \n I chose to use a travel agent. I have to say, she&#039;s amazing and has really been able to take care of all of the details for us.  We have people traveling from all around the country and wanted someone who would be able to help coordinate with everyone&#039;s schedules.  She sends me updated listings everytime someone books and at any point in time, I can tell who is coming, when, how many rooms we have booked in total, etc. She has been a life saver and would definitely using a travel agent.\n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]ThomasK[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Hello All \n \n \n I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It&#039;s looks [b]amazing[\/b]!) \n \n \n We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we&#039;re shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning. \n \n One thing we&#039;re already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA. \n \n \n Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons? \n \n We&#039;ve been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief. \n \n I&#039;ve just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA. \n \n Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited! \n \n Thanks and best regards \n \n \n - TK[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1588492,"PostDate":1330544109,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Hi TK!<\/p> <p> <br \/> I chose to use a travel agent. I have to say, she's amazing and has really been able to take care of all of the details for us.\u00a0 We have people traveling from all around the country and wanted someone who would be able to help coordinate with everyone's schedules.\u00a0 She sends me updated listings everytime someone books and at any point in time, I can tell who is coming, when, how many rooms we have booked in total, etc. She has been a life saver and would definitely using a travel agent.<br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>ThomasK<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Hello All<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It's looks <strong>amazing<\/strong>!)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we're shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> One thing we're already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons?<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We've been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I've just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thanks and best regards<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> - TK<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"floresvy05@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1260154781,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-223750.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Vanessa56","Id":223750,"Name":"Vanessa56","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f40cda03e3c9d615b8c4cba6b19c94f3","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Hi All,&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I know there are a lot of former NOW Sapphire brides and soon to be NOW Sapphire brides on this board. Since Paradisus Riviera was bought out and changed names to NOW Sapphire, there haven&#039;t been a lot of reviews on weddings at the hotel.&amp;nbsp; I greatly appreciate the information the former brides have posted on this thread, and I was wondering if any of you would mind doing a formal review of the hotel and your wedding.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Thank you! =)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1588497,"PostDate":1330544478,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Hi All,<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I know there are a lot of former NOW Sapphire brides and soon to be NOW Sapphire brides on this board. Since Paradisus Riviera was bought out and changed names to NOW Sapphire, there haven't been a lot of reviews on weddings at the hotel.\u00a0 I greatly appreciate the information the former brides have posted on this thread, and I was wondering if any of you would mind doing a formal review of the hotel and your wedding.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thank you! =)<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"floresvy05@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1260154781,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-223750.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Vanessa56","Id":223750,"Name":"Vanessa56","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0d3984ee4d4553265fef15c6bb468995","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I am on my 16 day countdown!!!!  &amp;nbsp; &lt;span alt=\":woot:\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/woot.gif\"&gt;&lt;img height=\"27\" id=\"yui_3_4_1_2_1330573695165_151\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/woot.gif\" width=\"42\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; ....sorry I just had to shae it with someone!!&amp;nbsp; HeHe!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1588762,"PostDate":1330577472,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I am on my 16 day countdown!!!!\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <span alt=\":woot:\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/woot.gif\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' height=\"27\" id=\"yui_3_4_1_2_1330573695165_151\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/woot.gif\" width=\"42\" \/><\/span><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> ....sorry I just had to shae it with someone!!\u00a0 HeHe!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ladybug1280@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1284746058,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232417.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AmyG","Id":232417,"Name":"AmyG","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"db437f07df95cdfb00a320e3f4c1b7f2","RawContent":"Hey ThomasK, \n \n   \n CONGRATS on your engagement and chosing the Now Sapphire.  I have had a great planning experience with this resort so far....I will surely post a review when I return \n \n I did go with a local travel agent in my town and he was great!  He really took over the planning for all travel arrangements for my guests.  In my Save the Dates I put my travel agents info and let people know that if they didn&#039;t already have a travel planner, they could use my guy.  \n My agent was able to negotiate better rates then what the resort offered at the time and he also held a block of rooms for me which I don&#039;t think I would have been able to do myself.  I just personally went with a travel agent because I knew that I did not want to be the &#039;go to person&#039; for everyone&#039;s questions aboout travel and stuff. \n \n I&#039;m sure which ever you choose will work out fine.  Happy Planning!!!! \n \n [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]ThomasK[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Hello All \n \n \n I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It&#039;s looks [b]amazing[\/b]!) \n \n \n We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we&#039;re shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning. \n \n One thing we&#039;re already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA. \n \n \n Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons? \n \n We&#039;ve been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief. \n \n I&#039;ve just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA. \n \n Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited! \n \n Thanks and best regards \n \n \n - TK[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1588768,"PostDate":1330578056,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Hey ThomasK,<\/p> <p> <br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <p> CONGRATS on your engagement and chosing the Now Sapphire.\u00a0 I have had a great planning experience with this resort so far....I will surely post a review when I return<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I did go with a local travel agent in my town and he was great!\u00a0 He really took over the planning for all travel arrangements for my guests.\u00a0 In my Save the Dates I put my travel agents info and let people know that if they didn't already have a travel planner, they could use my guy.\u00a0<\/p> <p> My agent was able to negotiate better rates then what the resort offered at the time\u00a0and he\u00a0also held a block of rooms for me which\u00a0I don't think I would have been able to do myself.\u00a0 I just personally went with a travel agent because I knew that I did not want to be the 'go to person' for everyone's questions aboout travel and stuff.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I'm sure which ever you choose will work out fine.\u00a0 Happy Planning!!!!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>ThomasK<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Hello All<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It's looks <strong>amazing<\/strong>!)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we're shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> One thing we're already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons?<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We've been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I've just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thanks and best regards<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> - TK<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ladybug1280@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1284746058,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232417.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AmyG","Id":232417,"Name":"AmyG","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3b989b18a2272539a1dcaa1030c9bd64","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Hi Thomas,&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Have you seen this thread about the NOW webinar we will be hosting:&amp;nbsp;&lt;img alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/&gt;\n \n &lt;p&gt; Hello All&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It&#039;s looks &lt;strong&gt;amazing&lt;\/strong&gt;!)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we&#039;re shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; One thing we&#039;re already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons?&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; We&#039;ve been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I&#039;ve just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Thanks and best regards&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; - TK&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;\/blockquote&gt; \n \n &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1588773,"PostDate":1330578586,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Hi Thomas,<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Have you seen this thread about the NOW webinar we will be hosting:\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Hello All<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I have been around these forums for different resorts for a few months now, but my fiance and I have finally decided that we want our wedding to be at the NOW Sapphire (It's looks <strong>amazing<\/strong>!)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We are quite a ways away from our wedding (we're shooting for july 2013) so we are in the absolute beginning of our wedding planning.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> One thing we're already both having trouble deciding on is should we go through a Travel Agent, or just go through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Which have you gone through? Which do you recommend i.e. pros\/cons?<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We've been talknig to a travel agent since early January of this year, but he seems to be slow on the response-sde of communication, which if Im going to have 40 people traveling to a different country and he is supposed to be \"taking care\" of everything for my guests...then that does not give me a feeling of relief.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I've just heard that travel agents can \"negotiate\" better deals with resorts as opposed to going through AAA.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Any and all helpful types\/information will be GREATLY apprecaited!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thanks and best regards<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> - TK<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Founder and Owner of BestDestinationWedding.com \u00a0\/ \u00a0<\/span><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78931-bride-and-groom-fly-free-20152016\/'><strong><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Bride & Groom Fly FREE Promotion<\/span><\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<br><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/wrighttravelagency.com\/inquiry\/'><span style=\"color:#008080;\">Looking for a travel agency that specializes in Destination Weddings<\/span><\/a><\/strong><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><strong>?<\/strong> \u00a0We are an award winning travel agency and you can <\/span><strong><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/reviews\/p\/21494-wright-travel-agency-destination-wedding-and-honeymoon-specialists\/'><span style=\"color:#008080;\">read our reviews\u00a0here.<\/span><\/a><\/strong><\/span><br>\n\u00a0<br><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><strong>Awards and recognition:\u00a0<\/strong><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Palace Resorts PRO Platinum Agency (Top Award) \u00a0 \u00a0 | \u00a0 \u00a0<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">AMResorts Master Agent & Top Agency \u00a0<\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Karisma Hotels Diamond Level 5 (highest production), Top 10 Azul Weddings, Top Wedding Coordinator | <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/68050-karisma-hotels-givc-and-gi-wedding-consultants-wright-travel-agency\/'><strong>Wright Travel & Karisma GIVC Benefits<\/strong><\/a><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Travel Impressions Best of the Best Globe Winner \u00a0 \u00a0| \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Apple Vacations Golden Apple Winner \u00a0<\/span><\/span><br><img src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17572\/gallery_206696_17572_8409.jpg\" alt=\"gallery_206696_17572_8409.jpg\"> \u00a0 \u00a0<img src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17572\/sml_gallery_206696_17572_1003.jpg\" alt=\"sml_gallery_206696_17572_1003.jpg\"><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><strong><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/921\/vendor-business-membership-fees-rules-updated-6-18-2010'>Vendor rules are HERE! Please read!<\/a>\u00a0\u00a0<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#b22222;\">If you are a vendor and looking to advertise your business,<\/span>\u00a0please email\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='mailto:ads@bestdestinationwedding.com?subject=Advertising%20on%20BestDestinationWedding.com'>ads@bestdestinationwedding.com<\/a>.<\/strong>","Email":"admin@bestdestinationwedding.com","IpAddress":"71.202.225.11","GroupId":4,"GroupName":"Administrators","JoinDate":1137227820,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-206696.jpg?_r=1386394555","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":135,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TammyWright","Id":206696,"Name":"TammyWright","IsOnline":true}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":2541,"TotalPages":255,"CurrentPage":260,"NextPage":270,"PreviousPage":250,"LastPage":2540},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
