{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"33c6420841e65b6a57c9654669fd29c8","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Our Wedding on the Tequila Terrace at NOW Sapphire, Mexico on 6.2.2012&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; We spent 10 days at NOW Sapphire to celebrate our wedding, which took place on June 2, 2012. I received so much helpful information from this discussion board that I wanted to share my experiences too. I waited to post this until everything was over because I think hindsight is helpful. So, below is a lengthy (sorry!) account of my experience as a NOW Sapphire bride:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; First, some context about me as a bride: I had a budget. My husband and I paid for our own wedding. I am a relaxed traveler and try very hard not to sweat the small stuff. When we decided to have a destination wedding I embraced the following philosophy: \u00e2\u20ac\u0153Live in the moment. Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t sweat the small stuff. Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t stress about the big picture.\u00e2\u20ac\u009d I am so glad I did because it allowed me to make plans for my day, including particular details that were important to my husband and I, without worrying about every little thing the day of.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; We used our local travel agent, Mary Ann Downey, at Rainbow Travel in Harrison City, PA. We distributed her information to all of our guests in our homemade save the date cards (this is one place we saved a TON of $$-- see photos below) and everyone loved her. She was a joy to work with! She booked us through Apple Vacations (we\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve used them on several occasions and have never been disappointed) and our guests through Apple and Go Go Worldwide, depending on who was running a promotion and had the lower price. I know that using a travel agent made it possible for more of our guests to attend because 1) she was aware of lower prices and 2) they didn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t have to pay for everything up front. When you use a travel agent you make a deposit and have a due date for the rest of the money owed. Many of our guests made payments throughout the year\u00e2\u20ac\u201dessentially making our wedding a part of their monthly billing cycle. This would not have been possible without Mary Ann!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"\" src=\"data:image\/jpeg;base64,\/9j\/4AAQSkZJRgABAQEASABIAAD\\\/2P\\/j5+v\/AABEIAPABQAMBIgACEQEDEQH\/2wCEAAICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgQDAgICAgUEBAMEBgUGBgYFBgYGBwkIBgcJBwYGCAsICQoKCgoKBggLDAsKDAkKCgoBAgICAgICBQMDBQoHBgcKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCgoKCv\/aAAwDAQACEQMRAD8A\/Mna15pqK3EkICjPOD+PuM10+mOP7FiYjLokiqCeTh2GfocjmuV01Cs1zCv+rmTeyDP0\/XOfwq1a3TxwvAx2eU6kZI5GSSR+fSvtN7LdJ3\/r+mevzdSEQtLMsYznG2PacEY\/+vWzdQpBIYoT\/wAe1sI8N3lc4579D1NaGiWwEdxfyjaIlxHnjceCx\/Dt9acLUlBLLJ81zeGfsf3ahiP5Djt0rppTle8Xt+L\/AKVvmRPl3ZNoUYRr26GwK7bF4+6BgH8OP0qsiAy20DEsqM0sjufX8O+T1rdW3ki0KKNUKfaZQrMzfdUncw4\/3cfiazbKNpZ7iTGDvWOIdl52k9\/UflXq4OrH3pp9f+B\/mcdRuyjb+t2b103l2hjUfffAUZ+ViMDnv97\/AMdNM0K1V7qPC5jidrjbn+FBhcD3OPzp1+rlIsPzlhGM8gklUDD2y34JWpp8AXTZXh3br+XyYyMbVhT77de2G\/TvXrQruMeVNX1\/H+mc7jreXT+vzIpZGnkhwwLTykoVX72Wwp+mO\/8AjWwlpa28McbsPMZ\/9dGOrZ5\/DBx+FZlsFX7TqDjbFGRDap2LDHzZ79xxULSahlbiWGeOI\/LveJgD3x35xg\/SvaoVW9IvRfn5ehyVnCPx63\/I9V0lmttNeOZ1JeMAFSDnMmAf\/rV2Ol3MhjmtpBGS0R2EeqAYHX3z9RXnWi3r3mlLIfk8tCjHjgq6Y4P+8K7HTJETUsH5f9JZSdo6FePwywr3I4qyjfRr\/h3+J5bpxUnbZ\/5\/5Hd6Tdm8hDBzHJnDYYZUqenvzg13unTNbQMXkSafeOSeWcn\/ABx\/kV4tDey6Vqj\/ACMbZ5S+GPqOo\/NeO\/416JoOoLqFzEoc7LfEjEoBu7Y574bNfQ0cXaPNdcu\/\